    "created_at": "2016-06-30T01:29:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-30T01:29:34Z",
    "body": "So what I did is, explicitly overriding the viewport's scrollbar style (without touching anything else) when the fullscreen element is neither null nor the root. (Code and comment can be found [here](https://dxr.mozilla.org/mozilla-central/rev/b69a5bbb5e40bd426e35222baa600b481e50d265/layout/base/nsPresContext.cpp#1420-1424))\n\nSo `overflow` of `<body>` would be propagated to viewport as normal if `<html>` has its default value of `overflow`, but if we are in fullscreen, even if the `overflow` is `scroll`, the viewport would behave as if it is `hidden`. I'd propose we add this behavior to the spec.\n\nThe wording could probably be: when the fullscreen element is neither null nor the root element, the computed value of viewport's `overflow` property is ignored, and `hidden` is used instead.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/fullscreen/issues/comments/229536220/reactions",
      "total_count": 0,
